\f1\fs22 At home, Chanta waved his armpit at the front lock and pushed the door open. As soon as he was closeted in the tiny hall, he kicked off his shoes. The still air told him he was alone. He sighed with relief.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He and Andrea had been fighting for weeks. Not just raised voices, not only verbal abuse, but physical assaults: mostly knees to the groin and hair-pulling, Andrea the aggressor in every case. Chanta had no taste for violence. It left him sick, and Andrea rampant. Andrea wanted commitment, which Chanta interpreted as his commitment to accepting her more percussive affections.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With beer in mind, Chanta went to the kitchen. A video on the stasis closet\'92s door began to play; he\'92d triggered its proximity sensors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> It was Andrea. \'93I put myself up for random allocation,\'94 the video said. Andrea\'92s image planted her fists on her hips and jutted her jaw out in defiance.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93So what?\'94 Chanta said to the rotting bananas in a bowl by the jar of whey protein. Both sat atop the cooking hubs, which neither he nor Andrea ever used. \'93That\'92ll take forever, if it happens at all.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Andrea beamed out of the stasis closet and Chanta\'92s heart chilled.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A table of data appeared, covering Andrea\'92s torso. Chanta was annoyed he could no longer see her tits. The table scrolled and highlighted a row. There was her name, Andrea Novetine, matrimonially allocated with a dude named James Marrin in holy joint venture.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He\'92s an Information Integrity Manager,\'94 she boasted from the closet\'92s surface, and Chanta felt flatter than her cold image. \'93I\'92m moving up. Boy, what was I thinking? A cleaner?\'94 She laughed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta decided on affirmative proactiveness, then wondered if proactiveness was a real word.\
