<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He\'92s already in search-and-destroy mode,\'94 Major said. Chanta rolled his eyes and nodded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93C\'92mon, Halo,\'94 Abe said. \'93Chanta\'92s here.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Can\'92t talk. Hunting,\'94 Halo replied in psycho-killer monotone. The others laughed; Halo was a riot.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Say hello, Halo,\'94 pleaded Abe. \'93Think of Chanta. He\'92s single again. He needs cheering up.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Andrea is a fake Stacy bitch,\'94 Halo said. \'93She deserves to die.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>In spite of the crowd, the music, and the gaming machines, silence descended around their table.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eventually, Halo broke his trance and lightened up. \'93Never be sad,\'94 he told Chanta. \'93Your friends are looking after you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Andrea doesn\'92t matter,\'94 Chanta said. \'93I met the perfect woman today.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Two o\'92clock!\'94 Halo said, scrambling to the dance floor.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There he goes,\'94 Major said with dismay. \'93He\'92ll score again for sure.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What\'92s he got that I haven\'92t?\'94 Abe challenged.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta and Major let the awkward silence swell and even refrained from sipping their frothy brews.\
